          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "This dashboard watches the jobs that **exist**. It cannot watch the ones that do not.\n\nPer `docs/design/tsd-backups-and-monitoring.md`, the lab still has **no image backup and no offsite copy** \u2014 `pg_dumpall` protects against an accidental `DROP`, not against losing the disk. That spec is parked on a ~$50 USB SSD. Until it unparks, a green row here means \"the one backup we have ran\", not \"the lab is recoverable\".\n\nOff-box coverage lives in Healthchecks: `heartbeat.sh`, `repo-sync.sh` and `pg-backup.sh` each ping on every run, so silence \u2014 the one signal a dead box can still send \u2014 is alerted from outside.",
